      "biography": "Sukhwinder Singh was born in India and rose to fame as a playback singer in Bollywood. He gained widespread recognition with his song 'Chaiyya Chaiyya' from the film Dil Se, which showcased his powerful vocal abilities and unique style. Over the years, he has established himself as a leading voice in Indian cinema, performing a wide range of songs from romantic ballads to energetic dance numbers. His training in Indian classical music has greatly influenced his singing technique and style.",
