      "is_group": false,
      "biography": "Born in Mumbai, India, Shankar Mahadevan showed an early interest in music and trained in both Carnatic and Hindustani classical traditions. He rose to prominence as a playback singer in the 1990s and later became a successful composer and part of the Shankar-Ehsaan-Loy trio. His career spans various genres including classical, pop, and fusion, and he has won numerous awards for his singing and composing. He is also known for his teaching and promotion of Indian music globally.",
      "known_for": "Known for his powerful and versatile vocal abilities, blending classical Indian music with contemporary styles, and his role in the Shankar-Ehsaan-Loy trio.",
      "start_year": 1990,
      "description": "Shankar Mahadevan is a renowned Indian singer and composer, famous for his work in Indian classical music as well as playback singing in Bollywood and other Indian film industries. He is a founding member of the Shankar-Ehsaan-Loy musical trio, which has composed music for numerous successful films. His vocal style blends classical Indian techniques with contemporary music, making him a versatile and influential figure in Indian music.",
